efferson-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs from 1951 to 2025, 75 years, and on the middle of the county&rsquo;s grids October to November came in under 90% of normal in 39 of them. In 2025, March to April hit 269% of normal on the middle of the grids and November to December fell to 48%. May to June is the wettest pair at 8.83 inches of normal. Grid 17228 had its driest year in 2011 at 54%.</p>"}
